.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt REC 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rec
.Nd record audio through OSS with a live level meter
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Ar file
.Op Ar effect Op Ar arguments ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs sox_ng in recording mode.
It reads from the OSS sound device,
.Pa /dev/dsp
by default, and writes an audio file.
WAV is built in; external codec libraries are disabled.
Options and effects are those of
.Xr sox 1 .
.Pp
.Fl S
shows progress and the live recording level on standard error.
.Fl r Ar rate ,
.Fl c Ar channels
and
.Fl b Ar bits
select the recording format.
Use
.Cm trim 0 Ar seconds
after the output file to stop after a given duration.
Without it, interrupt the recording with Ctrl-C to finish the file.
.Pp
Select the recording source and level with
.Xr mixer 1 .
The device determines which rates, sample formats and channel counts
are available.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width AUDIODEV
.It Ev AUDIODEV
OSS device path, in place of
.Pa /dev/dsp .
.It Ev AUDIODRIVER
Set to
.Cm oss
to select OSS without probing for a default output first.
.It Ev SOX_OPTS
Default options, processed before the command line.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Record five seconds of signed 16-bit stereo WAV at 48000 Hz,
showing the level:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
rec -S -r 48000 -c 2 -b 16 take.wav trim 0 5
.Ed
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mixer 1 ,
.Xr play 1 ,
.Xr sox 1 ,
.Xr soxi 1 ,
.Xr dsp 4
